# Signing keys. *.p8 is an Apple Sign In private key — unencrypted, downloadable
# exactly once, and able to mint client secrets for the whole developer team until
# revoked. It has been sitting outside this repo since 2026-08-06 and was flagged
# twice without being fixed; one `git add -A` is all that stands between a stray
# copy and a committed credential. The others are the same class of mistake.
*.p8
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.aab
*.ipa
google-services.json

*.pid

# Deployment targets configuration
deploy-targets.conf

# Local Claude Code agent worktrees (temporary)
.claude/worktrees/

# Private Agent and Workspace Configurations (ignored in public repository)
.agents/
!.agents/workflows/
!.agents/skills/
.claude/
HANDOVER.md
SECURITY-AUDIT.md


# Agent scratch space — review diffs, generated reports, throwaway scripts. Kept on disk,
# never in the repo. Swept into #151 by a `git add -A`; ignored so it cannot recur.
scratch/

# Federation operator harness: holds TEST identity PRIVATE KEYS. Never commit.
scripts/federation/fed-state.json
